# rotator-cog — the names this cog reads. Names only: the values live in
# Doppler (rotator-cog / dev locally, prd deployed). Run under
# `doppler run -- …`; do not copy this to .env — nothing reads it.
#
# Uncommented names are required in Doppler's dev config, and
# `uv run check-doppler-keys` checks dev holds every one. Commented names
# are optional: the code has a default, or only the deployed worker reads
# them. In production the Lambda gets these from SSM (secrets) and its
# function environment, both declared in mini-app-polis/infra.

# external tooling: read by miniapppolis-common-utils' KaianoApiClient.
# This cog's own API key: the worker records each rotation and the sweep
# reads the rotation record as the rotator-cog machine. There is no
# fallback to another key — unset means every call to the API is a 401
# and no rotation is ever recorded. It is itself in the inventory, so the
# rotator rotates its own key like any other machine's.
ROTATOR_COG_API_KEY=

# external tooling: read by miniapppolis-common-utils' KaianoApiClient.
# Base URL of api-kaianolevine-com. Production reads the unsuffixed name,
# every other environment reads the _DEV one, and there is no fallback
# between them: a dev process with this unset stops posting rather than
# posting to production.
KAIANO_API_BASE_URL_DEV=
# KAIANO_API_BASE_URL=

# external tooling: read by miniapppolis-common-utils' init_sentry and
# logger. Sentry DSN for error tracking (unset turns Sentry off), and the
# log level: DEBUG, INFO (default), WARNING.
# SENTRY_DSN_COGS=
# LOGGING_LEVEL=

# The daily sweep rotates what is due only when this is "true". Unset, it
# retires previous keys and reports what is due and any drift, nothing more
# (src/rotator_cog/worker.py).
# ROTATOR_SWEEP_ROTATE=
# The sweep asks for a task per due manual secret only when this is "true".
# Unset, it reports which are due, so the first ask can be checked.
# ROTATOR_SWEEP_TASKS=

# Deployed worker only: the Parameter Store paths of the rotator's own
# Doppler and Railway tokens, one per config. The paths are set as plain
# function environment in mini-app-polis/infra; the tokens themselves are
# never in Doppler or any environment.
# DOPPLER_TOKEN_PRD_PARAMETER=
# DOPPLER_TOKEN_DEV_PARAMETER=
# RAILWAY_TOKEN_PRD_PARAMETER=
# RAILWAY_TOKEN_DEV_PARAMETER=

# Deployed worker only: the account and widget sitekey whose Turnstile
# secret the worker rotates through Cloudflare (src/rotator_cog/turnstile.py).
# Plain function environment set in mini-app-polis/infra; read only when a
# Turnstile rotation runs.
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
# TURNSTILE_SITEKEY=

# Deployed worker only: the JSON map of the secrets the function loads from
# Parameter Store at its first import (src/rotator_cog/__init__.py). Set by
# mini-app-polis/infra; unset, nothing is loaded.
# SSM_PARAMETERS=

# scripts/rotate.py only: the AWS CLI profile it rotates IAM keys with
# (default miniapppolis), and the login name it records as the rotation's
# actor when git has no user.email.
# AWS_PROFILE=
# USER=
